        "id": 1305927
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-06T20:57:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the transition from Attached.SNK to Error Recovery (or any CC open state), which is the one we care about here, this setting will have already happened in `tc_attached_snk_exit`. This one would be redundant, and we could avoid it by caching the ADD state.\n\n(We might also be able to avoid it by getting rid of one of the calls to `tcpm_enable_auto_discharge_disconnect`, but I suspect that would be unsafe. I\u0027m guessing there\u0027s a reason we call this in both places.)\n\nThe appropriate place to do that caching would probably be in `tcpci_tcpc_enable_auto_discharge_disconnect`.\n\nSince your current change defers 2-4 register accesses, and caching would avoid 1-2, I would expect caching to save about half as much time as what you\u0027re doing now.",
      "revId": "d2f3f5d7710455d4646fd28d7d165f3c5bac0c20",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
